# Agent tools

- One tool per file (`<action>.tool.ts`), built with `defineTool` from `@/agent/tool`; snake_case name (`create_task`)
- Return JSON-serializable data; throw `Error` for expected failures — never format a protocol response
- `summarize` only on write tools (becomes a chip in the chat UI); reads don't have it
- Tools and domains NEVER import MCP/OpenAI: the MCP SDK only lives in `agent/mcp-server.ts`; OpenAI's only in `integrations/openai.ts`
- Same JSDoc habit as routes: title / blank / `` `snake_case_name` `` / blank / description / `@returns` (and `@param` only if useful). Official tone — no "template/example"
- `execute` body uses three section banners (same dash length as routes): `// -- Input ---`, `// -- Processing ---`, `// -- Output ---`. Input holds ctx/args locals; Processing holds repository/service work and throws; Output holds the return. Always include all three
- Canonical example: `apps/api/src/domains/task/tools/create-task.tool.ts`
